---
description: Rules when editing or creating Unity prefabs and assets
globs: **/Assets/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---

- NEVER edit metdata directly; use Unity CLI instead.
- Refer to `/unity-cli` skill for more information regarding Unity CLI.
- If user doesn't have Unity CLI, request user to install (see [here](docs.unity.com/en-us/unity-cli/use-unity-cli#install-with-a-package-manager])).
- If the environment is sandboxed (e.g: `The required instruction sets are not supported by the current CPU.`), request user to use Unity MCP, or unsandbox the agent (more dangerous approach).
- For prototyping assets from scratch, use `/asset-prototype` skill.
- For sprites, either width and height must be multiple of 4, or pack them in SpriteAtlas, or else no compression is applied.
- Provide visual checks for users to confirm if the assets look what user is expecting for.
- For fixed Unity UI, author containers, dimensions, alignment, and visual styling in prefabs and use serialized prefab references for repeated elements; do not derive sizing from runtime RectTransforms or force layout rebuilds unless requirements explicitly call for dynamic layout.
